{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01CapREq7uHrRG4BZ4H6vxcC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Q34 is done. The only remaining Next item is the validation step. That's the next task per the plan — completing it now would be the *second* unchecked item, so I stop here per the one-task-per-run rule.\n\n---\n\n**Completed:** `answers/02-034-weak-evaluation-hiding-retrieval-failures.md`\n\n**What's in the note:**\n- **Framing:** Targets mid/senior evaluation discipline — distinguishing engineers with real eval infra from vibes-based teams\n- **Concept:** Weak eval hides retrieval failures because LLMs paper over partial/irrelevant context, keeping end-to-end scores flat while root-cause retrieval issues accumulate\n- **Mechanism:** Two-layer golden-dataset framework — retrieval layer (Recall@5, NDCG, RAGAS `context_recall`) + generation layer (`faithfulness`, `answer_relevancy`); the diagnostic split between them tells you exactly which layer is broken\n- **Example:** Legal-tech case where semantic chunking cut NDCG from 0.72 → 0.51 but end-to-end LLM-judge stayed at 84% for 6 weeks before a production incident\n- **Pitfalls:** Using thumbs-up as sole metric; treating RAGAS as a single score; spot-checking 10 queries per sprint; skipping production cosine-score telemetry\n- **Related:** Q21 (full eval framework), Q13 (6 RAG failure modes), Q33 (embedding drift)\n\nNext plan item: `validate — run: bash ralph-ai-engineering/validate.sh 02-rag-systems`"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":335,"cache_read_input_tokens":61710,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":335,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cc882a6b-962c-4239-b772-349876981514","uuid":"d9472756-b169-418f-9c5b-d98cc8305aad"}
